+---
+name: private-fund-memo
+description: Run local evidence-backed private fund PDF QA and generate source-traceable investment memo PDFs from native PDF files in this project.
+allowed-tools: Bash(cd:*), Bash(python:*), Bash(curl:*), Bash(test:*), Bash(ls:*), Bash(find:*), Bash(rg:*), Read, Glob, Grep
+when_to_use: Use when the user asks for private fund research, local PDF QA, investment memo generation, source-backed answers, citations, traceability, due diligence, or a memo similar to the provided report PDF. Trigger phrases include "私募研究", "PDF问答", "基于这个PDF回答", "生成memo", "投资memo", "可溯源", "same memo", "research memo", and "用本地PDF".
+argument-hint: "[pdf_path] [company] [ticker] [question-or-memo-request]"
+arguments:
+  - pdf_path
+  - company
+  - ticker
+  - request
+---
+
+# Private Fund Memo
+
+Use this workflow to answer questions against a local PDF and generate a source-traceable private-fund investment memo PDF.
+
+## Inputs
+
+- `$pdf_path`: Absolute path to the local source PDF. If omitted, use the active registered PDF if one exists; otherwise use `/Users/Admin/project/private_fund_ai_research/tesla_extracted/20260129_10-K_0001628280-26-003952.pdf`.
+- `$company`: Company name. Infer from the filename or user message when obvious; otherwise ask a short clarification.
+- `$ticker`: Public ticker. Infer from the filename or user message when obvious; otherwise ask a short clarification.
+- `$request`: User question or memo request.
+
+## Goal
+
+Produce a chat answer and, when requested, a report-style memo PDF with traceable evidence. The final response must include the generated PDF path, citation ids or source pages, and any review caveats.
+
+## Rules
+
+- Use the existing direct native-PDF flow. Do not build a chunk index unless the user explicitly asks for chunking or indexing.
+- Use local PDF evidence before outside knowledge. Do not invent facts, page numbers, source paths, or citation ids.
+- Every material investment claim should be backed by a citation id, page reference, or generated trace.
+- If the PDF is scanned, unreadable, missing, or insufficient for the question, say so and mark the result as needing review.
+- Keep all user-facing workflow in the single Omnigent chat box; do not introduce a separate private-fund frontend panel.
+
+## Steps
+
+### 1. Resolve Inputs
+
+Change to the project root:
+
+```bash
+cd /Users/Admin/project/private_fund_ai_research
+```
+
+Confirm the PDF exists:
+
+```bash
+test -f "<pdf_path>"
+```
+
+If the user provided the NVIDIA example path, use that exact path and infer company/ticker as `NVIDIA Corporation` / `NVDA`. If the user did not provide a PDF, use the default Tesla 10-K path and infer `Tesla, Inc.` / `TSLA`.
+
+**Success criteria**: The selected PDF path exists, and company/ticker are known.
+
+### 2. Run Direct PDF QA And Memo Generation
+
+For a one-shot answer plus memo PDF, run:
+
+```bash
+python scripts/run_pdf_research_demo.py \
+  --pdf "<pdf_path>" \
+  --company "<company>" \
+  --ticker "<ticker>" \
+  --question "<request>"
+```
+
+The script extracts native PDF text, answers against page-paragraph evidence, generates citations, and renders a memo PDF under `/Users/Admin/project/private_fund_ai_research/output/pdf`.
+
+**Success criteria**: The command returns JSON containing `qa.answer`, `qa.citations`, `memo.memo_id`, and `memo.pdf_path`.
+
+### 3. Use Omnigent API When A Live Chat Session Needs Stateful QA
+
+If the Omnigent server is running and the user wants multiple follow-up questions against the same PDF, register the PDF once:
+
+```bash
+curl -sS -X POST http://127.0.0.1:6767/v1/private-fund/pdf/register \
+  -H "content-type: application/json" \
+  -d '{"pdf_path":"<pdf_path>","company_name":"<company>","ticker":"<ticker>"}'
+```
+
+Ask follow-up questions:
+
+```bash
+curl -sS -X POST http://127.0.0.1:6767/v1/private-fund/pdf/ask \
+  -H "content-type: application/json" \
+  -d '{"question":"<question>","top_k":3}'
+```
+
+Generate the memo:
+
+```bash
+curl -sS -X POST http://127.0.0.1:6767/v1/private-fund/memo/generate \
+  -H "content-type: application/json" \
+  -d '{"company_name":"<company>","ticker":"<ticker>"}'
+```
+
+**Success criteria**: API responses contain citations/traces for QA and `pdf_path` plus `pdf_url` for memo generation.
+
+### 4. Return The Result
+
+Summarize in Chinese by default:
+
+- Answer the user's question directly.
+- Include 2-5 key evidence references, using citation ids or page references from the run.
+- Include the generated memo PDF absolute path.
+- Mention whether LLM drafting was used and whether any section needs review.
+- If the command failed, report the failing step and the shortest actionable fix.
+
+**Success criteria**: The user can open the memo PDF path locally and see which sources back the answer.
+
+## Output Shape
+
+Use this shape for final chat replies:
+
+```text
+已完成。基于 <company> (<ticker>) 的本地 PDF，我生成了可溯源回答和 memo PDF。
+
+回答：<concise answer with citation ids>
+
+Memo PDF：<absolute pdf path>
+引用：<citation/page summary>
+需复核：<yes/no and why>
+```
